15:| term attack roll meaning | An attack roll is a D20 Test for an attack with a weapon, an Unarmed Strike, or a spell. | R-GLOS-004 | GLOSSARY.md |
17:| term cantrip meaning spell level slot | A cantrip is a level 0 spell cast without a spell slot. | R-GLOS-006 | GLOSSARY.md |
18:| term Concentration meaning | Concentration is the sustained attention some spells and effects require to remain active; losing it ends the effect. | R-GLOS-007 | GLOSSARY.md |
22:| term spell slot meaning | A spell slot represents a limited portion of a spellcaster's magical potential used to cast level 1+ spells. | R-GLOS-011 | GLOSSARY.md |
32:| warlock pact magic how many slots what level; warlock 5 spell slots; pact slot progression same level; warlock slot table | Pact Magic slots are ALL one shared level: 1 slot of level 1 at Warlock 1, 2 slots from Warlock 2, with the slot level rising to 2/3/4 at Warlock levels 3/5/7 — Warlock 5 has exactly two level-3 slots and nothing lower. | R-CLASS-004 | R_CLASSES.md |
48:| what happens without armor or Shield training; can you cast spells | Without training in worn Light, Medium, or Heavy armor, you have Disadvantage on D20 Tests involving Strength or Dexterity and cannot cast spells; without Shield training, its AC bonus does not apply. | R-COMBAT-014 | R_COMBAT.md |
66:| can I ready a spell readied spell slot lost concentration casting time | Only a spell with a casting time of an action; the slot is expended when you ready it, holding it requires Concentration up to the start of your next turn, and broken Concentration wastes the spell. | R-COMBAT-032 | R_COMBAT.md |
67:| can I ready a bonus action prepare a bonus action with a trigger healing word misty step | No; Ready accepts only an action or movement, and no rule grants a Bonus Action in response to a trigger, so bonus-action spells cannot be readied at all. | R-COMBAT-033 | R_COMBAT.md |
71:| magic initiate which spell lists cantrips; magic initiate spellcasting ability int wis cha; is magic initiate ability forced by list | Magic Initiate: learn two cantrips from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list, and the feat's spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma — chosen FREELY when the feat is selected, not forced by the list. | R-FEAT-002 | R_FEATS.md |
72:| magic initiate level 1 spell free cast per day; magic initiate spell always prepared; can magic initiate spell use spell slots; recharge short or long rest | Magic Initiate's level 1 spell is always prepared, castable ONCE without a spell slot per Long Rest, and ALSO castable with any spell slots the character has. | R-FEAT-003 | R_FEATS.md |
75:| can a feat be taken twice; repeatable feats list; take magic initiate twice; stack alert or savage attacker | A feat can be taken only once unless it has a 'Repeatable' subsection; in feats.txt those are exactly Magic Initiate (different spell list each time), Skilled, and Ability Score Improvement. | R-FEAT-006 | R_FEATS.md |
92:| paladin ranger half caster multiclass spell slots round up or down; does a 1-level paladin dip give slots | HALF, ROUNDED UP. Paladin 1 or Ranger 1 contributes a FULL caster level, same as a Wizard dip. | R-MC-001 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
93:| which classes count full toward multiclass spell slots caster level | Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard — every level counts. | R-MC-002 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
94:| can multiclass slots be higher level than any spell you know or prepare; what are the extra slots for | Yes, and they are usable only to UPCAST spells you actually prepare. Five 1-level full-caster dips = caster level 5 (slots 4/3/2) while preparing only 1st-level spells. | R-MC-003 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
95:| which spellcasting ability applies to a multiclass prepared spell | The ability of the class the spell is associated with — each prepared spell belongs to one class. | R-MC-004 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
99:| do warlock levels count toward multiclass spell slots; is pact magic added to the shared slot table; warlock dip caster level | NO. The Spell Slots total names Bard/Cleric/Druid/Sorcerer/Wizard in full and Paladin/Ranger at half rounded up. Warlock is ABSENT, so every Warlock level contributes ZERO shared slots; Pact Magic is a wholly separate pool. | R-MC-008 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
100:| can a multiclass character prepare 3rd level spells; what level spells can each class prepare; multiclass prepare higher level spells; level 1 dip what spells | Preparation is PER CLASS, as if single-classed at that class's level. A level-1 class prepares ONLY level-1 spells; a level-3 full caster prepares up to level 2 (SRD example: level 3 Sorcerer, "spells of level 1 or 2"). Preparing a LEVEL-3 spell requires one FULL-CASTER class at level 5+ (full casters gain 3rd-level slots at class level 5; half-casters not until class level 9). Shared multiclass slots above a class's cap exist for UPCASTING only (see R-MC-003). | R-MC-009 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
104:| how many spells can I prepare; prepared spells number formula ability modifier plus level; prepared spells column class table multiclass | The NUMBER of prepared spells is the fixed Prepared Spells column of that class's own Features table, per class as if single-classed (Ranger 4 prepares 5, Sorcerer 3 prepares 6, Cleric 5 prepares 9) — NOT ability modifier + class level, and never one combined count per character. | R-MC-013 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
105:| when do paladin and ranger get spellcasting; half caster spells at level 1 or 2; level 1 paladin dip spell slots prepared spells | In SRD 5.2.1 Paladin and Ranger have the Spellcasting feature at CLASS LEVEL 1: each level-1 row grants 2 prepared spells and 2 level-1 spell slots. | R-MC-014 | R_MULTICLASS.md |
111:| what interrupts a Short Rest; Initiative spell damage | Rolling Initiative, casting a spell other than a cantrip, or taking any damage stops the Short Rest and it grants no benefits. | R-REST-006 | R_RESTS.md |
115:| when do ordinary Spellcasting spell slots return | Finishing a Long Rest restores all expended Spellcasting spell slots, unless a specific feature says otherwise. | R-REST-010 | R_RESTS.md |
118:| how many Pact Magic spell slots does a Warlock have and what level are they; warlock slot level progression 1 2 3 5 7 9 | From the Warlock table's own columns: 1 slot of level 1 at Warlock 1; 2 slots from Warlock 2; slot LEVEL rises to 2 at 3, 3 at 5, 4 at 7, 5 at 9. | R-REST-013 | R_RESTS.md |
128:| when do elven lineage and fiendish legacy spells arrive; elf tiefling species spells level 3 5 character level or class level; misty step darkness free casting long rest | At TOTAL CHARACTER levels 3 and 5 (never at level 1, never class level) each lineage/legacy spell is always prepared, castable once per Long Rest without a slot, and also castable with any appropriate-level slot — Drow Faerie Fire/Darkness, High Elf Detect Magic/Misty Step, Wood Elf Longstrider/Pass without Trace, Abyssal Ray of Sickness/Hold Person, Chthonic False Life/Ray of Enfeeblement, Infernal Hellish Rebuke/Darkness. | R-SPECIES-001 | R_SPECIES.md |
129:| what spellcasting ability do species trait spells use; elven lineage gnomish lineage fiendish legacy otherworldly presence save DC intelligence wisdom charisma chosen or class ability | A CHOSEN ability — Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma, picked when the lineage/legacy is selected — not the character's class spellcasting ability. | R-SPECIES-002 | R_SPECIES.md |
134:| do cantrips scale on class level or total character level in multiclassing | TOTAL CHARACTER level, unless the spell says otherwise. | R-SPELL-001 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
135:| can slots above your known or prepared spell level cast higher-level spells | No. Higher-level slots can only cast and potentially enhance lower-level spells you actually prepare. | R-SPELL-002 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
136:| how many Magic Missile darts; how many with a level 4 spell slot | Three darts at level 1, plus one dart per slot level above 1; a level 4 slot creates SIX darts. | R-SPELL-003 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
137:| where do single-class spell slot counts and levels come from; full caster half caster progression | A single class uses its Features table; multiclass shared slots count every Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, and Wizard level plus half of each Paladin and Ranger level rounded UP, then use the Multiclass Spellcaster table; Pact Magic is separate. | R-SPELL-004 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
138:| what does upcasting do automatically; does every spell gain damage or targets | The spell takes on the slot's higher level, but it gains extra effects only when its description says so. | R-SPELL-005 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
139:| can you concentrate on two spells or effects at once; when does new concentration end old concentration | No. Starting another Concentration spell or effect immediately ends the current Concentration. | R-SPELL-006 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
142:| how does ritual casting work; prepared required; extra time; spell slot cost | Under the general rule, a Ritual-tagged spell must be prepared, takes 10 minutes longer, and expends no spell slot; a specific feature can override the preparation requirement. | R-SPELL-009 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
143:| can a ritual spell be cast at a higher level or upcast | No. Because the Ritual version expends no slot, it cannot be cast at a higher level. | R-SPELL-010 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
144:| when can each class change prepared spells; preparing versus knowing spells 2024 | Bard, Sorcerer, and Warlock replace one when gaining a class level; Cleric, Druid, and Wizard replace any after a Long Rest; Paladin and Ranger replace one after a Long Rest. | R-SPELL-011 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
145:| do always-prepared spells count against number of prepared spells | No. An always-prepared spell does not count against a changeable prepared-spell list's limit. | R-SPELL-012 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
146:| how to calculate spell save DC and spell attack bonus | Spell save DC = 8 + spellcasting ability modifier + Proficiency Bonus; spell attack bonus = spellcasting ability modifier + Proficiency Bonus. | R-SPELL-013 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
147:| can you cast two leveled spells in one turn; Bonus Action spell and action spell 2024 | On a turn, you can expend only ONE spell slot to cast a spell; cantrips and slotless casting do not expend a slot. | R-SPELL-014 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
148:| must a Wizard prepare a Ritual spell in the spellbook to cast it as a Ritual | No. Ritual Adept lets a Wizard cast a Ritual-tagged spell from their spellbook without preparing it, but they must read from the book while casting. | R-SPELL-015 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
149:| wizard prepare spells from spellbook or full wizard spell list; wizard long rest replacement pool; what spells can a wizard prepare | On gaining a Wizard level, a Wizard REPLACES prepared spells only with spells recorded in their spellbook — the spellbook, not the full class list, is the replacement pool. | R-SPELL-016 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
150:| how many spells can a cleric druid paladin prepare; prepared spells formula ability modifier plus level; where does prepared spell count come from | Prepared-spell counts are FIXED numbers read from each class's Features table Prepared Spells column with no ability-score dependence; e.g. Cleric 1 prepares exactly 4 spells (with 3 cantrips and 2 level-1 slots), Cleric 3 prepares 6. | R-SPELL-017 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
151:| warlock pact magic how many slots what slot level; warlock 3 5 7 spell slots; pact slot progression table levels 1-7 | Pact Magic slots are few and ALL of one slot level from the Warlock table: Warlock 1 has 1 slot of level 1; Warlock 2 has 2 of level 1; Warlock 3-4 have 2 of level 2; Warlock 5-6 have 2 of level 3; Warlock 7-8 have 2 of level 4. | R-SPELL-018 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |

