.ai/rules/R_FEATS.md:27:TRAP: Forgetting the slot-casting clause: a Fighter gets exactly 1/day, but a Wizard Acolyte can additionally burn slots on it. The free use recharges on LONG Rest only, not Short. It does not count against a class's prepared-spell limit (see R-SPELL-012).
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:143:| can a ritual spell be cast at a higher level or upcast | No. Because the Ritual version expends no slot, it cannot be cast at a higher level. | R-SPELL-010 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:144:| when can each class change prepared spells; preparing versus knowing spells 2024 | Bard, Sorcerer, and Warlock replace one when gaining a class level; Cleric, Druid, and Wizard replace any after a Long Rest; Paladin and Ranger replace one after a Long Rest. | R-SPELL-011 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:145:| do always-prepared spells count against number of prepared spells | No. An always-prepared spell does not count against a changeable prepared-spell list's limit. | R-SPELL-012 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:146:| how to calculate spell save DC and spell attack bonus | Spell save DC = 8 + spellcasting ability modifier + Proficiency Bonus; spell attack bonus = spellcasting ability modifier + Proficiency Bonus. | R-SPELL-013 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:147:| can you cast two leveled spells in one turn; Bonus Action spell and action spell 2024 | On a turn, you can expend only ONE spell slot to cast a spell; cantrips and slotless casting do not expend a slot. | R-SPELL-014 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:148:| must a Wizard prepare a Ritual spell in the spellbook to cast it as a Ritual | No. Ritual Adept lets a Wizard cast a Ritual-tagged spell from their spellbook without preparing it, but they must read from the book while casting. | R-SPELL-015 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:149:| wizard prepare spells from spellbook or full wizard spell list; wizard long rest replacement pool; what spells can a wizard prepare | On gaining a Wizard level, a Wizard REPLACES prepared spells only with spells recorded in their spellbook — the spellbook, not the full class list, is the replacement pool. | R-SPELL-016 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:150:| how many spells can a cleric druid paladin prepare; prepared spells formula ability modifier plus level; where does prepared spell count come from | Prepared-spell counts are FIXED numbers read from each class's Features table Prepared Spells column with no ability-score dependence; e.g. Cleric 1 prepares exactly 4 spells (with 3 cantrips and 2 level-1 slots), Cleric 3 prepares 6. | R-SPELL-017 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:151:| warlock pact magic how many slots what slot level; warlock 3 5 7 spell slots; pact slot progression table levels 1-7 | Pact Magic slots are few and ALL of one slot level from the Warlock table: Warlock 1 has 1 slot of level 1; Warlock 2 has 2 of level 1; Warlock 3-4 have 2 of level 2; Warlock 5-6 have 2 of level 3; Warlock 7-8 have 2 of level 4. | R-SPELL-018 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:152:| do paladins get cantrips 2024; ranger cantrips srd; half caster cantrips known; paladin sacred flame legal | NO cantrips for Paladin or Ranger at ANY level in SRD 5.2.1 — their Features tables have no Cantrips column at all; a mutt's cantrips come only from full-caster classes, species traits, or feats. | R-SPELL-019 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:153:| true strike 2024 what does it do; true strike attack and damage ability; true strike radiant scaling components | True Strike (Divination cantrip; Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard; Action; S, M — a proficient 1+ CP weapon, NO Verbal): make one weapon attack using your spellcasting ability for BOTH attack and damage rolls instead of Str/Dex; damage can be Radiant or the weapon's type; extra Radiant 1d6 at character level 5 (2d6 at 11, 3d6 at 17). | R-SPELL-020 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:154:| shillelagh damage die casting time ability; shillelagh d8 scaling levels 5 11 17; does recasting shillelagh end the old one | Shillelagh (Druid cantrip, BONUS ACTION, 1 minute): a held Club or Quarterstaff attacks with your spellcasting ability instead of Strength and its damage die becomes a d8 (d10 at character level 5, d12 at 11, 2d6 at 17); damage can be Force or the weapon's normal type; ends early if you cast it again or let go of the weapon. | R-SPELL-021 | R_SPELLCASTING.md |
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:219:- **R-FEAT-003** — Forgetting the slot-casting clause: a Fighter gets exactly 1/day, but a Wizard Acolyte can additionally burn slots on it. The free use recharges on LONG Rest only, not Short. It does not count against a class's prepared-spell limit (see R-SPELL-012).
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:288:- **R-SPELL-010** — Treating the extra 10-minute casting time as permission to choose a higher spell level.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:289:- **R-SPELL-011** — Using the 2014 vocabulary split where Bard, Sorcerer, and Warlock "know" spells while only some classes prepare them. SRD 5.2.1 calls all of these prepared spells and varies replacement cadence.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:290:- **R-SPELL-012** — Counting subclass, species, background, or feat spells against a class's prepared-spell allowance merely because they appear in the same sheet section.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:291:- **R-SPELL-013** — Adding the full ability score, using class level for proficiency, or assuming every multiclass spell uses the same spellcasting ability.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:292:- **R-SPELL-014** — Applying the 2014 Bonus Action spell restriction. SRD 5.2.1 instead limits the number of spell slots expended to cast spells on a turn.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:293:- **R-SPELL-015** — Applying the general prepared-spell requirement without the Wizard feature's specific exception.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:294:- **R-SPELL-016** — R-SPELL-011 gives the Wizard's replacement CADENCE (any, after a Long Rest) but not the POOL; recall pattern-matches Wizard onto Cleric/Druid and prepares from the whole class list, producing an illegal prepared list of spells never scribed.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:295:- **R-SPELL-017** — Using the 2014 formula (class level + ability mod). It coincides with the table at some levels — a Wis 16 Cleric 3 gives 6 both ways — and diverges elsewhere (Wis 20 Cleric 1: formula 6, table 4), so agreement at one level proves nothing.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:296:- **R-SPELL-018** — R-MC-008 establishes Pact Magic is separate from shared slots but records no slot COUNT or LEVEL; recall substitutes a full-caster spread (e.g. 4/2 at Warlock 3) or wrong slot level, mispricing every slot round and short-rest recovery in the sim.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:297:- **R-SPELL-019** — Full-PHB recall grants Paladins cantrips via the Blessed Warrior fighting style — that is NOT SRD content, and a drafted entry here originally QUOTED it from memory; the citation gate caught the fabrication. Proven by ABSENCE, hence CHECK not QUOTE, with the Sorcerer header as the positive control.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:298:- **R-SPELL-020** — Recall of 2014 True Strike (advantage on your next turn, no attack) is a completely different spell; and the ability substitution applies to the DAMAGE roll too, not just the attack roll — a sim rolling Str/Dex and omitting the level-5 +1d6 Radiant gets both numbers wrong.
.ai/rules/INDEX.md:299:- **R-SPELL-021** — 2014 recall keeps the Wis-based attack but forgets the die upgrade to d8 and the 5/11/17 die scaling, or spends an Action instead of a Bonus Action — wrong die, wrong attack bonus, wasted action. Source is column-interleaved here: the d8/Force sentences are split by blank right-column lines ("becomes" and "a d8." are separated), so longer spans need CHECK-style short phrases.

